<title>BELGIUM: EU to discuss grain needs of remote regions.</title>
<headline>EU to discuss grain needs of remote regions.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union's cereals management committee will on Thursday discuss the grain needs of the Canary Islands, Madeira and the Azores in 1997/98 (July/June), EU member state officials said.</p>
<p>Grain shipments to these remote Spanish and Portuguese islands benefit from EU export refunds.</p>
<p>The needs of French overseas departments such as Martinique and Reunion will be discussed at a later date.</p>
<p>-Brussels newsroom +322 287 6830</p>
</text>
